{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"agent_message","text":"The failure mode is clearer now: when an expression is typed as a union but codegen still has a raw primitive value, `gen_assign_cast` tries to box using the union type itself. Union reach types do not have a primitive layout, so the box path returns `NULL`. I’m checking the `as`/call/return code paths to make sure the tuple fix is using the right static element type."}}
